From dda56bfbf7f62db9eb0c23b633b4a4d5e618fbe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 05:52:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] httpd: one-file full backup/restore (settings + Reaper
 stores); diag v1.3.6

Backlog P2: the stock Save-setting file is only the nvram blob, and every
Reaper list moved to /jffs (v2.6.3-v2.6.9) - a stock backup + reset +
restore silently lost the Gatekeeper device list, firewall lists, routing
rules and Warden cache. One archive now carries both halves:

  REAPER-BACKUP 1 + meta line + the stock .CFG (byte-identical HDR2+JCFG
  format, still restorable by stock/Merlin) + the v2.7.0 reaper_cfg JSON +
  the fqdn ipset cache (domain objects come back populated).

- Download: GET /REAPER_<model>_<ver>_settings.rbk (do_reaper_fullbak_file;
  the URL names the file, same trick as Settings_<model>.CFG; .rbk added to
  httpd's handler-generated whitelist). CFG produced exactly as prf_file's
  default branch (rbk_make_cfg).
- Restore: multipart reaper_restore.cgi validates EVERYTHING first (magic,
  meta, model vs productid, /jffs health gate, the CFG part's own HDR
  magic, the JSON parses, the fqdn part is well-formed) and only then
  writes: JSON parked at /jffs/reaper/restore_pending.json (fw/pbr drafts
  live on tmpfs and would not survive the reboot), fqdn cache laid down,
  CFG to /tmp/settings_u.prf and the stock do_upload_config() path replays
  it (jffs cfgs + nvram restore + commit + reboot). A failed check changes
  nothing.
- After the reboot one click completes the Reaper half (action=pending /
  import_pending, the import core refactored into rcfg_import_json; lists
  stage as drafts behind commit-confirm exactly as an interactive import).
- UI: injected card on the stock Administration page (mode-4 block in
  reaper_inject.c fetches the tokenized fragment Reaper_BackupCard.asp and
  wires it - stock page stays byte-pristine); pending-restore banner also
  on the Storage page. 14 new RBKP_ tokens, 25 dicts lockstep 6759.
- reaper_diag v1.3.6: churn rate no longer ~0/h when the log head carries
  pre-NTP timestamps (span starts at the first credible timestamp; slow
  loops shown per-day); duplicate 14d mangle REAPER_PBR line removed.
- rtrafd: db_align logs the cursor alignment (field diagnostic + verify
  marker).

Host-validated: injected card JS + Storage page JS parse clean; rtrafd
harness still 9/9; diag sh -n clean; dicts lockstep 6759 x25.
