 RWDN_90=(unnamed)
 RWIF_83=Error
 RWIF_84=block
+RBKP_1=Full backup (settings + Reaper data)
+RBKP_2=One file that carries everything: the router settings file the buttons above save, plus the Reaper stores that live outside it - the Gatekeeper device list, the firewall lists and their domain-set cache, the routing rules, and the Warden lists. The stock file inside stays readable by stock and Merlin firmware.
+RBKP_3=Download full backup
+RBKP_4=Restore full backup...
+RBKP_5=Restore checks that the file matches this router model, restores the router settings, and reboots. After the reboot, log back in and click Complete restore when prompted - firewall and routing lists are staged for review on their pages, never applied blind.
+RBKP_6=A full-backup restore is waiting to finish its Reaper half.
+RBKP_7=Complete restore
+RBKP_8=That backup was made on a different router model.
+RBKP_9=The /jffs storage is not healthy, so the Reaper half cannot be restored. Run the diagnostic, fix storage, then try again.
+RBKP_10=Restoring - the router settings are being applied and the router will reboot. Log back in and click Complete restore when prompted.
+RBKP_11=Restore completed: %1 setting(s), %2 list(s), %3 rejected. Firewall and routing lists are staged - apply and keep them on their pages.
+RBKP_12=Not a Reaper full-backup file.
+RBKP_13=Restore this full backup? The router settings will be replaced and the router will reboot.
+RBKP_14=The restore failed. Nothing was changed.
